{"repositoryId":16730829,"availability":"available","full":"mathiasbourgoin/Sarek","name":"Sarek","description":"SIMT Abstractions for Runtime Extensible Kernels (GPGPU programing with OCaml)","category":"Other","language":"OCaml","stars":149,"forks":12,"created":"2014-02-11T13:00:37Z","updated":"2026-10-18T15:16:43Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"http://mathiasbourgoin.github.io/Sarek/","topics":["cuda","gpgpu","ocaml","opencl","spoc"],"demo":"https://mathiasbourgoin.github.io/Sarek/playground.html","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:03.019Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:03.019Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:03.019Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T18:05:03.019Z","stars":149,"forks":12}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["SIMT Abstraction for Runtime Extensible Kernels","Sarek is a PPX-based DSL that lets you write GPU kernels directly in OCaml syntax. Kernels compile to multiple backends (CUDA, HIP, OpenCL, Vulkan, Metal) without code changes, plus WGSL for the browser and two CPU backends.","Sarek is the user-facing DSL and compiler. Write kernels in OCaml with [%kernel ...], and Sarek compiles them to GPU code at build time."],"features":["Kernels compile to multiple backends automatically without code changes.","The CUDA family registers as two frameworks (CUDA/PTX and CUDA/C); use Device.filtercuda () to match both.","The published backend page is stale against the two tables above, and is deliberately not linked from them. gh-pages/docs/backends.md — which is what mathiasbourgoin.github.io/Sarek/ serves — still has a single CUDA row…","Type Safety: GADTs and phantom types for compile-time guarantees","Zero-Copy: Efficient memory sharing between host and device"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mathiasbourgoin/Sarek/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a6bf93ca78b1f77e1c115924d043e9f35ca4226af092ccb0eb65a9e045b531dd","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:03.121Z"},"overviewCh